{"name":"Glossy Black","hex":"#110011","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glossy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a smooth, silklike, reflective (shiny) surface.","Attention-grabbing and superficially attractive."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A glossy magazine.","A glossy photograph."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glossy"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gloss (optics)","blocks":[{"text":"Gloss is an optical property which indicates how well a surface reflects light in a specular (mirror-like) direction. It is one of the important parameters that are used to describe the visual appearance of an object. Other categories of visual appearance related to the perception of regular or diffuse reflection and transmission of light have been organized under the concept of cesia in an order system with three variables, including gloss among the involved aspects. The factors that affect gloss are the refractive index of the material, the angle of incident light and the surface texture."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Gloss_light_Illuminates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gloss_(optics)","wikidata":"Q900581"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Nanorough.gif/330px-Nanorough.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Nanorough.gif/330px-Nanorough.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Figure1: Specular reflection of light from a rough surface","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANanorough.gif"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Specular_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Specular_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpecular_gloss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Sheen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Sheen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASheen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/Contrast_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/Contrast_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AContrast_gloss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Absence_of_bloom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Absence_of_bloom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbsence_of_bloom.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Distinctness_of_image_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Distinctness_of_image_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistinctness_of_image_gloss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Gloss-samples.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Gloss-samples.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGloss-samples.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg/500px-Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg/500px-Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg"}],"sounds":{"glossy":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/En-us-glossy.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d6/En-us-glossy.ogg/En-us-glossy.ogg.mp3"}],"black":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8a/En-Black.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/8a/En-Black.ogg/En-Black.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/En-uk-black.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6d/En-uk-black.ogg/En-uk-black.ogg.mp3"}]}}}